, us-west, eu-west). Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that had been healthy, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back to v2.2.9 (the next most recent healthy production release) in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, version v2.2.9 in all regions, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: confirm the v2.2.9 rollback with the owning team, determine the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and decide on a fixed release path given the v2.3.0 quarantine.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2026-05"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002.\n\nI didn't roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The platform rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. v2.2.9 was the next most recent healthy release, so I used that. Since v2.2.9 was already healthy in production, this didn't need change-manager approval.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**, which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also lists follow-ups: confirming the v2.2.9 choice with the owning team, finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and deciding how to ship a fix now that v2.3.0 is quarantined.", "type": "text"}]}]}